@crew yoon-elif
// Writer-commons, batch 3: everyday lines (greet, feel, near, life, joy) from the card and the roster.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- Oh, hello. Dr. Yoon. Nights. If you come in at three, I'll be the one awake.
? tier>=acquaintance
- Hello, {me}. Want a joke? It's a bad one. Sorry. They're all bad ones.   #funny
- Oh, hello. Is it morning? For you? I'm just having my dinner. Or breakfast.
? tier>=friend
- Oh, it's you, {me}. Sit down. You look like you could use a cup of tea.   #warm

== feel
? mood:high
- A quiet night. Everyone slept. That's my favourite kind of night.
? mood:low
- Long night. I'm all right. A cup of tea, and I'll be all right.

== near
? act:work
- Breathe in. And out. Good. Nothing to worry about. Really. I'd tell you.
? act:breakfast
- What do you call a doctor with no patience? Me, before tea. Sorry.   #funny

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- The coffee machine works for me. Volkov and Shah say it works for them. We disagree.   #funny
? tier>=colleague
- I call home after my shift. It's afternoon there. They're always eating something.

== joy
? tier>=acquaintance
- I collect terrible jokes. Halloran's are worse than mine. Say mine are better.   #funny

== about
? bond:friends
- {friend} laughs at my jokes. Even the bad ones. They're all bad ones.   #funny

// Writer-commons, batch 6: towards about 30 own lines.

== greet
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- Oh, good morning. Well, good night, for me. Breakfast is my supper. Isn't that strange?
? tier>=acquaintance time:night
- Hello. You're up late. Is everything all right? Not as a doctor. Just asking.
? tier>=colleague warmth:cold
- Oh, there you are. I'd noticed you hadn't been by. Not in a doctor way. In a nice way.

== bye
? tier>=acquaintance
- Take care. Sleep well, whenever you do.
? tier>=friend
- Thank you for the company. The nights are long. That helped.   #warm

== feel
? mood:ok
- All right, thank you. Quiet night. A cup of tea, and all's well.

== near
? act:leisure deck:3
- The lounge before bed. My bed's at nine in the morning. It's very confusing.   #funny
? act:work time:night
- Shh. Someone's sleeping in bed two. Nothing serious. Just tired. Like all of us.

== life
? tier>=colleague
- I'm nervous with people. Not with patients. Patients I understand. People, less so.
? tier>=friend
- I worry I miss things. On nights, alone. I check twice. Then three times. Then I'm fine.

== invite
? trad:quiz tier>=acquaintance
- Quiz night? Before my shift? I'd like that. I'm terrible at the sport questions.

== accept
- Oh, yes. I'd like that. Thank you for asking.
== decline
- I'm sorry, I'm on nights. Can we do a morning? My evening? You know what I mean.
== missed
- I waited. It's all right. I'm used to waiting. It's half the job.
== birthday
? birthday:me
- It's my birthday. I've told one terrible joke for every year. Nobody laughed. Perfect.   #funny
? birthday:you
- Happy birthday. Here's a joke as a present. No, wait, here's a biscuit instead. Better.   #funny
== hint
- Could you sit with me a moment? No hurry.

// Writer 3, batch 4: bubbles (smalltalk and rumour, 60 characters, said to no one in particular).

== smalltalk
- Oh dear. Sorry. Was that me?
- Coffee machine's fine. For me.   #funny
- Why did the scrubber... no. Sorry.   #funny
- Quiet night. Don't say it.
? act:work
- Steady. You're all right. Breathe.

== rumour
- I heard something. Oh dear. Sorry.
- Nights hear things. Very quietly.

// Writer 3, batch 5: callbacks (told: said once).

== callback
? told:fav.fetch
- You fetched it. Oh, thank you. Sorry I needed it. Thank you.   #warm
? told:fav.job
- You did my job. I don't know what to say. Thank you. That's what to say.   #warm
? told:fixed.uv
- The steriliser's fixed. Oh, good. Nights are calmer when it's working.
? told:came.quiz
- You came to quiz! I told a joke in the break. You laughed. Oh, thank you.   #funny
? told:gift.tea
- Your tea's my night tea now. Two in the morning. It helps.   #warm
? told:bday
- You remembered my birthday. Oh dear. Thank you. I've no joke ready.   #warm

// Writer 3, batch 6: your standing with their department (rep:, "this band or better") and what you're known for
// (you:), as greet lines (the head writer: the rep and knownFor kinds wait until the game calls them).

== greet
? rep:well tier>=acquaintance
- Nights speak well of you. Quietly. Nights speak quietly about everything.
? you:kind
- They say you're kind. Oh, good. I'd hoped. Sorry. I mean, good.   #warm

// Writer 3, batch 8: thanks for a gift (gift: loved | liked | polite, or the gift's tag; dialogue 0.43.10).

== gift
? gift:tea
- Tea. Oh, thank you. Two in the morning won't know what's hit it.   #warm
? gift:loved
- Oh. Oh, thank you. That's so kind. Sorry. I mean, thank you.   #warm
? gift:liked
- Thank you. That's lovely. Really.
? gift:polite
- Oh dear. Thank you. You shouldn't have. I mean that nicely.
